WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:02.360
SAST ownership should be explicit.

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:10.740
Someone must own tool configuration, rule governance, scan coverage, onboarding, exception review, reporting, and improvement.

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:17.920
Security teams may guide rules and risk interpretation, but developers and application owners need responsibility for fixes.

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:21.420
Platform or DevOps teams may own pipeline integration.

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:25.320
Governance keeps the program from becoming a disconnected dashboard.

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:29.140
Metrics should measure risk reduction, not only finding counts.

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:40.080
Useful measures include scan coverage, language and repository coverage, finding aging, remediation trends, recurring root causes, exception trends, and time to fix high-risk findings.

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:49.580
A rising finding count may mean a program is discovering previously unseen risk, while a falling count may reflect real improvement or simply disabled rules.

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:51.560
Metrics need interpretation.

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:58.500
SAST findings should feed back into secure coding standards, developer education, threat modeling, and design review.

00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:06.400
If several teams make the same mistake, the answer may be a safer framework pattern, a shared library, a checklist update, or a training module.

00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:12.380
If a tool repeatedly misses an important class of issue, manual review or custom rules may need to cover the gap.

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:16.360
Continuous improvement keeps the program useful as systems change.

00:01:16.580 --> 00:01:21.540
Audit evidence and management reporting should support decisions without overwhelming engineers.

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:29.120
Leaders need to know whether important repositories are scanned, high-risk findings are aging, exceptions are controlled, and remediation is improving.

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:31.980
Developers need clear and timely feedback.

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:40.360
A mature SAST program connects both views: operational detail for teams, risk trends for governance, and evidence for stakeholders.
